{"timestamp":"2026-03-31T09:51:56Z","event_ts":"2026-03-31T09:51:37Z","repo":"oist/smartphone-robot-android","event_name":"issue_comment","action":"created","actor":"topherbuckley","run_id":"23791277272","run_attempt":"1","sender":{"login":"topherbuckley","html_url":"https://github.com/topherbuckley"},"issue":{"number":51,"title":"Robot freezes without speed updated","state":"closed","html_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/51","milestone":null},"pull_request":null,"comment":{"id":4161349002,"html_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/51#issuecomment-4161349002","created_at":"2026-03-31T09:51:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T09:51:37Z","body":"Current evidence indicates this is not primarily an Android-app defect.\n\nThe Android-side freeze/crash is a downstream symptom of the firmware becoming unresponsive over serial after motor-driver / I2C lockup conditions. The active investigation is now being tracked in the firmware repo here:\n\n- oist/smartphone-robot-firmware#30\n  https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-firmware/issues/30\n\nClosing this Android issue in favor of the firmware tracker so the investigation stays attached to the likely root cause.\n"},"milestone":null,"changes":null,"severity":"INFO","target_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/51#issuecomment-4161349002","event_id":"34a87c7181840a6f219044aeb7d8b21f0881c983cf1275cba83d5afa672fbaca"}
{"timestamp":"2026-03-31T10:01:42Z","event_ts":"2026-03-31T10:01:25Z","repo":"oist/smartphone-robot-android","event_name":"issue_comment","action":"created","actor":"topherbuckley","run_id":"23791668740","run_attempt":"1","sender":{"login":"topherbuckley","html_url":"https://github.com/topherbuckley"},"issue":{"number":31,"title":"LiteRT migration","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/31","milestone":null},"pull_request":null,"comment":{"id":4161426917,"html_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/31#issuecomment-4161426917","created_at":"2026-03-31T10:01:25Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T10:01:25Z","body":"This issue appears already resolved by the TensorFlowLite2LiteRT milestone work rather than by the current issue-fix PR.\n\nVerified references:\n- tekkura/sr-android#162 created the migration guide\n- tekkura/sr-android#183 added the inventory of prior TensorFlow Lite usage\n- tekkura/sr-android#185 implemented the migration to MediaPipe/LiteRT-backed APIs\n- tekkura/sr-android#191 fixed the guide/version follow-up\n- tekkura/sr-android#220 merged the completed milestone into main\n\nCurrent repo state also reflects the migrated path:\n- MediaPipe `tasks-vision` is the active dependency\n- `ObjectDetectorData.kt` uses MediaPipe object detection APIs rather than the old TensorFlow Lite runtime path\n\nClosing as already handled by the TensorFlowLite2LiteRT milestone.\n"},"milestone":null,"changes":null,"severity":"INFO","target_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/31#issuecomment-4161426917","event_id":"b113c7f58afc892767b2e02ed6684664e4d99440075e7152b03cc18d2af69b61"}
