{"timestamp":"2026-03-31T10:01:43Z","event_ts":"2026-03-31T10:01:26Z","repo":"oist/smartphone-robot-android","event_name":"issue_comment","action":"created","actor":"topherbuckley","run_id":"23791669020","run_attempt":"1","sender":{"login":"topherbuckley","html_url":"https://github.com/topherbuckley"},"issue":{"number":43,"title":"Conflicting Namespaces in TensorFlow Lite Libraries","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/43","milestone":null},"pull_request":null,"comment":{"id":4161427011,"html_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/43#issuecomment-4161427011","created_at":"2026-03-31T10:01:26Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T10:01:26Z","body":"This issue appears already resolved by the TensorFlowLite2LiteRT migration work.\n\nThe original problem described a namespace conflict between old TensorFlow Lite artifacts (`tensorflow-lite-gpu:2.9.0` and `tensorflow-lite-api:2.8.0`). That dependency set is no longer present in the current repo.\n\nHistorical verification:\n- commit `5c684857` (`milestone/TensorFlowLite2LiteRT`) moved the project onto the MediaPipe/LiteRT-backed path and removed the old conflicting dependency setup\n\nCurrent repo state also reflects that:\n- MediaPipe `tasks-vision` is the active ML dependency\n- the old conflicting TensorFlow Lite dependency pair is no longer in the build config\n\nClosing as already resolved by the TensorFlowLite2LiteRT migration.\n"},"milestone":null,"changes":null,"severity":"INFO","target_url":"https://github.com/oist/smartphone-robot-android/issues/43#issuecomment-4161427011","event_id":"c94c13bada12b2b8bc093ffb1ebc8d018410c61a7460952a774321b000a0fc10"}
